          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Despite the size of the diagrams in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomGroupoidsOfPreSmoothGroupoids"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              by abstract coordinate charts to probes of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              by these charts, and take gauge transformations between these to gauge transformations between those, in a way that it compatible with changing probes along smooth maps.
          %p
            The following is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            in this context, and it says that this intuition in remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#YonedaIntuition"}
            is fully correct:
          #YonedaForPreSmoothGroupoids.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              defines a pre-smooth groupoid
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %munder
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo ̲
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underline{\mathbb{R}}^n
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PreSmoothGroupoid"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %munder
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo ̲
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underline{\mathbb{R}}^n \colon \mathbb{R}^k  \mapsto C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^k, \mathbb{R}^n)
                    \\in
                    Set
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    Grpd
            %p
              where the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              on the right is regarded as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              with only
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
              morphisms. This construction constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ̲
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PreSmooth
