            %p
              exhibiting the fact that smooth functions from an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              into a geometrically discrete space are constant on one of the points of this space, a situation which here is only refined by the fact that every morphism in the groupoid thus gives a
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
              between the two smooth functions that are constant on the two endpoints of this morphism.
          %p A particular case of this of special importance is this:
          #DeloopedGroupAsPreSmoothGroupoid.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet \in Grpd(Smooth0Type)
              for the Lie groupoid which
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi G
                      %mover
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟵
                            %mi i
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mo *
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet
                    \=
                    \\left(
                    G \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\stackrel{\overset{i}{\longleftarrow}}{\longrightarrow}}
                    \\ast
                    \\right)
            %p
              whose composition is the product operation in the group (the groupoidal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              of
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExternalYonedaEmbeddingsIntoPreSmooth1Type"}
              has groupoids of probes of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi disc
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n
                    \\mapsto
                    B \left(C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n,G)_{disc}\right)
            %p
              where on the right we have the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+1-type"} homotopy 1-type
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
              is that of smooth
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
          %p More specifically, the following class of examples plays a special role in the theory, as the encode what it takes for a pre-smooth groupoid to be a genuinely smooth groupoid.
          #GroupoidOfCover.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}_{i \in I}
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+groupoid"} Cech groupoid
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+groupoid"}> diffeological groupoid
              )
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})_\bullet
              whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  manifold of objects is
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ≔
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})_0 \coloneqq \underset{i \in I}{\coprod} U_i
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
                  of all the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charts"} charts
                  of the cover;
              %li
                %p
                  manifold of morphisms is
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ≔
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %munder
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})_1 \coloneqq  \underset{i,j \in I}{\coprod}U_i \underset{X}{\times} U_j
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
                  of all
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
                  of charts.
            %p
              and whose source, target and identity maps are the evident inclusions. There is then a
              %em unique
              composition operation.
            %p
              So a global point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \to C(\{U_i\})_\bullet
              may be thought of as a pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,i)
              of a point in the manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and a label
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              of a chart
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
              that contains it, and there is is precisely one morphism between two such global point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,i)\to (y,j)
              whenever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
              as well as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_j
              contain
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi j
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↗
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(\{U_i\})_\bullet
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; (x,j)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \nearrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    (x,i)
                    \&amp;&amp; \longrightarrow &amp;&amp;
                    (x,k)
                    }
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Under the embedding of example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExternalYonedaEmbeddingsIntoPreSmooth1Type"}
              there is an evident morphism of pre-smooth groupoids
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(\{U_i\})
                    \\longrightarrow
                    X
            %p
              from this Cech groupoid of the cover to the manifold that is being covered. This morphism simply forgets the information of which chart or intersection of charts a point is regarded to be in, and just remembers it as a point of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mi x
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ((x,i) \to (x,j))
                    \\mapsto
                    (x \stackrel{id_x}{\to} x)
                    \\,.
          #CechCoyclesAsSmoothMaps.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})
              the corresponding Cech groupoid, def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupoidOfCover"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
              its groupoidal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              according to example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeloopedGroupAsPreSmoothGroupoid"}
            %p
              Then the hom-groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PreSmooth1Type(C(\{U_i\}), \mathbf{B}G)
              of maps from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomGroupoidsOfPreSmoothGroupoids"}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  as
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cocycles
                  of degree 1 on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  relative to the cover and with values in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %munder
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi j
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        g_{ i j} \;\colon\; U_i \underset{X}{\times} U_j \longrightarrow G
                %p satisfying on each triple intersection the cocycle condition
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        g_{i j} g_{j k} = g_{i k}
              %li
                %p
                  as
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coboundaries"} coboundaries
                  between such cocycles
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{g_{i j}\}
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
