          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              It is a matter of unwinding the definitions that the statement holds disregarding smooth structure everywhere, hence after evaluating the morphisms of pre-smooth groupoids on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^0
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              for presheaves of sets on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
              (as discussed at
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets"} geometry of physics – smooth sets
          %h3#gluing Gluing
          %p
            The “bootstrap”-definition of pre-smooth groupoids
            %a{:href => "#PreSmoothGroupoids"} above
            works as intended, by prop.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#YonedaForPreSmoothGroupoids"}
            %em gluing
            of probes:
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a pre-smooth groupoid, then given a probe of it of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to X
            and given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to \mathbb{R}^n\}
            of the probe space by other probe spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \simeq \mathbb{R}^n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            from knowing its restrictions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{|U_i}\colon U_i \to X
            to these charts, and the information of how these are identified by gauge transformations on double overlaps.
          %p
            Such a system of local data and of gauge identification on double overlaps is just what maps out of the Cech groupoid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\})
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupoidOfCover"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CechCoyclesAsSmoothMaps"}
            for the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is of the form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeloopedGroupAsPreSmoothGroupoid"}
          %p
            In other words, the condition that smooth probes of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by coordinate charts
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            glue along covers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to \mathbb{R}^n\}
            of these charts is the condition that the groupoid of smooth maps out of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            itself
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R}^n \longrightarrow X
          %p is equivalent to the groupoid of maps out of the Cech groupoid of any cover
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C(\{U_i\}) \longrightarrow X
          %p
            and is so via the “restriction” map that takes the former and precomposes it with the canonical map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\}) \to \mathbb{R}^n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↗
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  C(\{U_i\}) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbb{R}^n
                  }
                  \\,.
          #DescentForPreSmoothGroupoids.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A pre-smooth groupoid
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi PreSmooth
                      %mn 1
                      %mi Type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in PreSmooth1Type
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PreSmoothGroupoid"}
              %em satisfies descent
              if for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              and for all differentiably
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+covers"} good open covers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to \mathbb{R}^n\}
              of the
              = succeed "-dimensional" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+chart"} coordinate chart
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X(\mathbb{R}^n) \simeq PreSmooth1Type(\mathbb{R}^n, X)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    PreSmooth1Type(C(\{U_i\}),X)
            %p
              given by pre-composition with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(\{U_i\}) \to \mathbb{R}^n
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+groupoids"} equivalence of groupoids
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              The condition in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DescentForPreSmoothGroupoids"}
              is called the
              = succeed "," do
                %em stack condition
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              “descends” down along the cover projection. So a smooth groupoid is a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              condition (see the next example) and hence a more systematic terminology would be to say that such
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sheaf"} 2-sheaf
              or rather a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-sheaf"} (2,1)-sheaf
              (since it takes values in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
              as opposed to in more general
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in PreSmooth0Type \hookrightarrow PreSmooth1Type
              be a pre-smooth groupoid which is really just a pre-smooth set, hence a presheaf on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
              that takes values in groupoids with only identity morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi op
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Grp
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \colon CartSp^{op} \longrightarrow Set \hookrightarrow Grp
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a smooth groupoid in the sense of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DescentForPreSmoothGroupoids"}
              precisely if it is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+set"} smooth set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              condition.
          #SmoothManifoldsSatisfyDescentAsPreSmoothGroupoids.num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              In particular, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SmoothMfd
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PreSmooth
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in SmoothMfd \hookrightarrow PreSmooth0Type \hookrightarrow PreSmooth1Type
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p
              There is an alternative formulation of the whole theory where instead of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              one uses the site
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothMfd"} SmoothMfd
              of all
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
              condition in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DescentForPreSmoothGroupoids"}
              is a much stronger condition.
            %p
              For instance the presheaves of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet = (G \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} \ast)
              from example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeloopedGroupAsPreSmoothGroupoid"}
              satisfy descent on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CartSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SmoothMfd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmoothMfd
            %p
              The choice of the smaller site is the one that is easier to work with, and therefore we stick with that. In fact, most every example of a pre-smooth groupoid that one runs into satisfies descent on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CartSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
          %p For example:
          #bfBGbulletSatisfiesDescent.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
