                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U \mapsto \Omega^1_{vert}(X \times U) // C^\infty(X\times U, U(1))
                    \\,.
          %p
            Such a structure
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            is a common joint generalization of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+groupoids"} discrete groupoids
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spaces"} smooth spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoids"} smooth groupoids
            %em
              %a{:href => "#SmoothGroupoids"} Smooth groupoids
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/centrally+extended+groupoid"} centrally extended groupoid
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+groups"} diffeological groups
            (such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+groups"} diffeomorphism groups
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+groups"} quantomorphism groups
          %ul
            %li#Souriau79
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marie+Souriau"}> Jean-Marie Souriau
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Groupes différentiels
              %em Differential Geometrical Methods in Mathematical Physics
              (Proc. Conf., Aix-en-Provence/Salamanca, 1979), Lecture Notes in Math. 836, Springer, Berlin, (1980), pp. 91–128. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=607688"}> MathScinet
              )
          %p The notion of smooth groupoids:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              , Def. 1.2.252 of:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.7930"}> arXiv:1310.7930
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Exposition of the concept of smooth groupoids motivated from basic
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
          %ul
            %li#Eggersson14
              Ragnar Eggertsson:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/bachelor+thesis+Eggertsson"} Stacks in gauge theory
              (2014)
          %p
            Discussion of smooth stacks as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spaces"} target spaces
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theories"} quantum field theories
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tony+Pantev"}> Tony Pantev
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Sharpe"} Eric Sharpe
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String compactifications on Calabi-Yau stacks
                %strong 733
                (2006) 233-296 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0502044"}> arXiv:hep-th/0502044
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#PantevSharpe
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tony+Pantev"}> Tony Pantev
